+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm start` to serve the site and `pnpm test` for the network helper tests.
+
+## Local resources
+
+Use **Connect to a local resource** to choose a local network device or a service on this computer, enter its HTTP(S) resource URL, and click **Connect**. No device requests run on page load. Only use read-only endpoints: the connector sends a GET request and displays the response as text.
+
+Deploy the site over HTTPS. Localhost development is a secure-context exception; serving over a plain HTTP LAN address is not. Browser local-network permission must be granted when requested. If blocked, change the site's local network or loopback permission in browser site settings.
+
+The target service must return an appropriate `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header for the website's origin. Browser permission does not replace CORS. No deprecated Private Network Access preflight handling is required. Connections omit credentials and reject redirects.
+
+The connector declares `targetAddressSpace` as `local` or `loopback`. Unsupported permission queries fall back to a user-initiated request; browser mixed-content and network restrictions may still prevent it. Use HTTPS on the local service if your browser blocks HTTP requests.
+
+If hosting inside a cross-origin iframe, the parent must delegate `allow="local-network; loopback-network"` and any parent `Permissions-Policy` must permit this app's origin. The app cannot override its parent's policy.
+
+Reference: [Local Network Access specification](https://wicg.github.io/local-network-access/).
